==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|es}} {{m|la|praestāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|praestō}}.

===Verb===
{{es-verb|prest|ar}}

# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[give]], [[pay]] {{gloss|e.g., attention}}
#: {{ux|es|¡'''Prestad''' atención, por favor!|translation=Pay attention, please!}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[lend]]
# {{lb|es|reflexive, transitive}} to have a natural inclination, a natural tendency
#: {{ux|es|El alcohol '''se presta''' al abuso.|translation=Alcohol tends to be abused.}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[take]]
#: {{ux|es|Los ministros '''prestan''' el juramento.|translation=The ministers take the oath.}}

====Conjugation====
{{es-conj-ar|prest|combined=1}}

